Z||000000||bHooper||03-31-2000||11:30 PM||||my buddy has a '84 SE, 4 spd with 115,000 miles on it.  this car idles at 5000 rpm!  any thoughts what could be causing this?  it does seem to drop a little when the vacum tube on the back side of the air cleaner is disconected  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||03-31-2000||11:53 PM||||After checking for ECM error codes.....<BR>check these......<P>Vac leaks. EGR jammed/bad. PCV valve bad. TBI unit loose at base or any where else. TBI gaskets bad. IAC bad. Static timing. (altho I don't think timing would push it to 5k it's still something to check and make sure its not part of it.)<P>FOR TESTING ONLY! You can disconnect the following lines and plug them on the TBI/Manifold ports to eliminate devices and their lines. The engine will run without these devices and not set ECM error codes.<P>Both Fuel Vapor canister lines.<BR>PCV line.<BR>Cruise control line.<BR>EGR line. (Check the EGR valve. if the pintle is not sealing then you still have a leak. remove the EGR and make a plate to cover the holes for testing if you aren't sure)<BR>Power Brake Booster line. (You may be able to just pinch a ruber section of this. be careful not to damage the line if you do.)<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 03-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||04-01-2000||09:58 AM||||interesting that you mention the brake booster line... he had to replace the booster several weeks ago, and then they went out agian yesterday!  we will give that a try first.<P>thanks, ogre!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ozzy||04-01-2000||01:14 PM||||In know the "duke" can be a pain but perservere. Mine ('88 Coupe) gave me a bunch of problems for a long time (huh ogre?) but although I thought they were all "Big" problems, in reality they all turned out to be simple and cheap to fix. <P>But in the process I have pretty much replaced every sensor, rebuilt the TBI, done the vacuum line stuff ogre described, redone the intake manifold gasket, K&N air filter & 165 degree thermostat etc, etc.<P>I have to say though I finally have this thing running so well I can hardly wait to drive it again. (NEVER thought that would happen!) I have put lottsa work into this car but it is finally beginning to pay off.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||04-01-2000||03:54 PM||||thanks, ogre.  we removed the bosster filter, it was clogged and filthy.  ||||reg||1
